# UPS support (IMG-06, #244): the ordered shutdown on a low UPS battery, started only by upsmon's SHUTDOWNCMD
# (onemind-ups-monitor.service), never at boot. onemind_ups.py: 1. apps (the k3s server stops so nothing restarts
# them, then every container gets SIGTERM and 30 s), 2. k3s (the container runtime left in its cgroup and its
# mounts), 3. the data volume (journal off /var/log, sync, stop data.mount, close the encrypted disk), 4. poweroff.
# No RequiresMountsFor=/data: stopping data.mount stops every unit that needs /data, and this one must keep going.
# Not sandboxed, on purpose: it stops k3s, kills its processes, unmounts /data and powers the box off.
# Time: onemind_ups.py starts poweroff within BUDGET (185 s) whatever hangs, and tries it twice (20 s each), so it
# ends before TimeoutStartSec. If it is still killed, or fails, FailureAction forces the poweroff: upsmon is gone
# by then (stopping data.mount stops it), so nothing else would power the box off before the battery dies.
[Unit]
Description=OneMind UPS: ordered shutdown on low battery (apps, k3s, data volume, poweroff)
DefaultDependencies=no
FailureAction=poweroff-force

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/lib/onemind/onemind-ups shutdown
TimeoutStartSec=240
